# skills/ is shipped wholesale via package.json `files: ["skills"]`, and an
# allowlisted directory is packed by walking it — a repository .gitignore does
# NOT prune inside it. Python bytecode from running the skill scripts locally
# therefore reached the tarball (27 `__pycache__/*.pyc` files in the v0.130.5
# dry-run). This file is the tarball-side counterpart of the root .gitignore.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
